(3092464, 432881, 32644, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very very much for the votes and the great feedback.<br/>I entered this in the diagonal challenge first but after a day I thought of this title and moved it to this challenge. Glad I did.<br/>I really thought the beach was too dirty to look really good but I see it was overlooked in favor of the subject - as I had hoped.<br/>WOW, I''m still pinching myself!</td>', 'Thank you all very very much for the votes and the great feedback.I entered this in the diagonal challenge first but after a day I thought of this title and moved it to this challenge. Glad I did.I really thought the beach was too dirty to look really good but I see it was overlooked in favor of the subject - as I had hoped.WOW, I''m still pinching myself!', '2006-12-06 11:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092476, 432458, 60862, '<td valign="top">Thanks, Gordon, for teaching me what a polarizer can do.  I would''ve voted higher had I known, but I''d still say it''s a little too colorful for a purely photography site.  I don''t know how to explain it better, but I''m looking for some realism in photos.  But as I said during the challenge, as an art piece it''s very pretty. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-06 11:12:00.</i></td>', 'Thanks, Gordon, for teaching me what a polarizer can do.  I would''ve voted higher had I known, but I''d still say it''s a little too colorful for a purely photography site.  I don''t know how to explain it better, but I''m looking for some realism in photos.  But as I said during the challenge, as an art piece it''s very pretty. :)', '2006-12-06 11:08:50.000000', '2006-12-06 11:12:00.000000', 0),
(3092489, 432784, 32644, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Beautiful shot! Your were definitely in the right place at the right time! This was one of my top picks too.<br/>Thanks for your comment on my red. It''s great to be a first timer, finally! You deserve it, too. Your work is very good.</td>', 'Congratulations! Beautiful shot! Your were definitely in the right place at the right time! This was one of my top picks too.Thanks for your comment on my red. It''s great to be a first timer, finally! You deserve it, too. Your work is very good.', '2006-12-06 11:15:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092506, 432140, 32644, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the yellow. This was one of my top picks too. I nearly fell off my chair laughing. You are a very clever guy and I love your work. Thank you too for the comments on my shot - they are very much appreciated.</td>', 'Congratulations on the yellow. This was one of my top picks too. I nearly fell off my chair laughing. You are a very clever guy and I love your work. Thank you too for the comments on my shot - they are very much appreciated.', '2006-12-06 11:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092513, 432140, 16241, '<td valign="top">funny photo, stunning venue. congrats</td>', 'funny photo, stunning venue. congrats', '2006-12-06 11:25:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092537, 432225, 51538, '<td valign="top">Came back to see how this photo did and where it was located.  Nice work.  Could have been higher in my opinion (which counts for little). ;-)</td>', 'Came back to see how this photo did and where it was located.  Nice work.  Could have been higher in my opinion (which counts for little). ;-)', '2006-12-06 11:34:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092545, 432929, 51538, '<td valign="top">The curve tells me a 5 point something.  So, we learn a thing or two. ;-)</td>', 'The curve tells me a 5 point something.  So, we learn a thing or two. ;-)', '2006-12-06 11:36:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092626, 432784, 69387, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I absolutely loved the colors of the sky and the reflection it bounced on the ground - breathtaking!</td>', 'Congratulations! I absolutely loved the colors of the sky and the reflection it bounced on the ground - breathtaking!', '2006-12-06 12:00:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092643, 432458, 656, '<td valign="top">Though it is real.  Get on a plane.  Hold a polariser up to your eye and look out the window.  That''s really what it looks like :)<br/> <br/>(I do know sort of what you mean but I have the same issues explaining it)<br/> <br/>It is real. It just looks very unnatural, even though it is entirely natural.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-06 12:04:56.</i></td>', 'Though it is real.  Get on a plane.  Hold a polariser up to your eye and look out the window.  That''s really what it looks like :) (I do know sort of what you mean but I have the same issues explaining it) It is real. It just looks very unnatural, even though it is entirely natural.', '2006-12-06 12:04:03.000000', '2006-12-06 12:04:56.000000', 0),
(3092661, 432140, 69387, '<td valign="top">Hilarious photo, serious background,  I love the contrast!</td>', 'Hilarious photo, serious background,  I love the contrast!', '2006-12-06 12:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092665, 432784, 48339, '<td valign="top">thanks for all the great comments!  it''s funny how the ''love hate'' relationship developed over the sky.  some loved it and some hated it.  the noise in the sky is a result of over editing and hue changes.  i don''t like it either, but i felt the resulting color change was more dramatic and worked well with my title.  i don''t know how i sneeked in at number one, but i''ll take my first ribbon and wear it with pride!  thanks everyone!</td>', 'thanks for all the great comments!  it''s funny how the ''love hate'' relationship developed over the sky.  some loved it and some hated it.  the noise in the sky is a result of over editing and hue changes.  i don''t like it either, but i felt the resulting color change was more dramatic and worked well with my title.  i don''t know how i sneeked in at number one, but i''ll take my first ribbon and wear it with pride!  thanks everyone!', '2006-12-06 12:12:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092692, 432619, 61012, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m surprised by the number of comments that either didn''t understand or said DNMC. It''s clear that those that made the comments of this nature didn''t recognize who Frida was. Before I read the title I knew that the image was inspired by her.<br/> <br/>I think your score relflects that same lack of recognition. I scored it as one of my top 10. I think it was terribly underrated.<br/> <br/>Keep-up the good work.</td>', 'Wow, I''m surprised by the number of comments that either didn''t understand or said DNMC. It''s clear that those that made the comments of this nature didn''t recognize who Frida was. Before I read the title I knew that the image was inspired by her. I think your score relflects that same lack of recognition. I scored it as one of my top 10. I think it was terribly underrated. Keep-up the good work.', '2006-12-06 12:24:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3092825, 431358, 23226, '<td valign="top">Believe it or not, we were only about 6 feet from the lion...literally. The only thing between my wife and I was a large guy with a rifle. We were on a safari in Zimbabwe, Africa. We had been trying to find lions all night long and stumbled on a pride of female lions. This one charged us several times. Pretty crazy.</td>', 'Believe it or not, we were only about 6 feet from the lion...literally. The only thing between my wife and I was a large guy with a rifle. We were on a safari in Zimbabwe, Africa. We had been trying to find lions all night long and stumbled on a pride of female lions. This one charged us several times. Pretty crazy.', '2006-12-06 12:58:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093111, 432784, 42100, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on winning the blue and your first ribbon on this wonderful photograph Brett!</td>', 'Congratulations on winning the blue and your first ribbon on this wonderful photograph Brett!', '2006-12-06 14:12:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093123, 432881, 42100, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on winning the red and your first ribbon Robin with this very emotive photograph.</td>', 'Congratulations on winning the red and your first ribbon Robin with this very emotive photograph.', '2006-12-06 14:15:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093135, 432140, 42100, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Sean on winning the yellow ribbon on this very funny and well executed photograph.  It seems as though you are quickly becoming the king of yellow ribbons.</td>', 'Congratulations Sean on winning the yellow ribbon on this very funny and well executed photograph.  It seems as though you are quickly becoming the king of yellow ribbons.', '2006-12-06 14:18:21.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3093170, 432881, 57162, '<td valign="top">Robin,<br/>Congrats on this excellent image, techically, artistically and emotionally.  Is it time to retire from WORK and start living you passion?  Miss talking to you at work.  <br/> <br/>Dave</td>', 'Robin,Congrats on this excellent image, techically, artistically and emotionally.  Is it time to retire from WORK and start living you passion?  Miss talking to you at work.   Dave', '2006-12-06 14:30:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093183, 432784, 16241, '<td valign="top">congrats on your first ribbon,  stunning shot.</td>', 'congrats on your first ribbon,  stunning shot.', '2006-12-06 14:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093197, 432912, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nefir:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks grainy and rather out of focus. I guess that''s what you see when you''re driving drunk!<br/> <br/>I wish this was composed better.. its an interesting idea.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>You seem you be the only one to get the idea ... I wanted this look a lot like what you''d see under those conditions.<br/> <br/>I <b>had</b> to shoot in tight (macro mode), since I was both modeling for and taking the shot -- with my left hand, crossed over. Sitting in the driver''s seat, there''s only a few inches between the lens and the wheel.<br/> <br/>With a one-second exposure, I was actually pretty impressed at how in-focus the top of the bottle came out; most of the rest is more OOF because of the shallow DOF.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nefir: Looks grainy and rather out of focus. I guess that''s what you see when you''re driving drunk! I wish this was composed better.. its an interesting idea. You seem you be the only one to get the idea ... I wanted this look a lot like what you''d see under those conditions. I had to shoot in tight (macro mode), since I was both modeling for and taking the shot -- with my left hand, crossed over. Sitting in the driver''s seat, there''s only a few inches between the lens and the wheel. With a one-second exposure, I was actually pretty impressed at how in-focus the top of the bottle came out; most of the rest is more OOF because of the shallow DOF.', '2006-12-06 14:36:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093203, 432140, 23430, '<td valign="top">Funny shot, and great composition too. Congrats on 3rd place.</td>', 'Funny shot, and great composition too. Congrats on 3rd place.', '2006-12-06 14:37:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093269, 432753, 67145, '<td valign="top">i reckon this should have done a whole heap better ... it''s miles ahead of so many others that were voted higher ... and even tho you didnt really know how the guy got hurt, your interpretation is valid as a message ... the expression on his face, taken together with the conversation he''s having on his fone, the ''headwear'' and the title is extremely emotive ...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-06 14:58:32.</i></td>', 'i reckon this should have done a whole heap better ... it''s miles ahead of so many others that were voted higher ... and even tho you didnt really know how the guy got hurt, your interpretation is valid as a message ... the expression on his face, taken together with the conversation he''s having on his fone, the ''headwear'' and the title is extremely emotive ...', '2006-12-06 14:56:58.000000', '2006-12-06 14:58:32.000000', 0),
(3093309, 432062, 50695, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 10s. Just a stunning shot. Do you see how other faces are formed in the texture of the wall, some using parts of the real faces that are showing through? remarkable.</td>', 'I was one of your 10s. Just a stunning shot. Do you see how other faces are formed in the texture of the wall, some using parts of the real faces that are showing through? remarkable.', '2006-12-06 15:08:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3093317, 431426, 50695, '<td valign="top">ths snapshot quality of this actually makes it more effective, because it seems more real. It''s the Blair Witch effect. Perfect expression and the hand on the hip really completes it. I gave this a 10.</td>', 'ths snapshot quality of this actually makes it more effective, because it seems more real. It''s the Blair Witch effect. Perfect expression and the hand on the hip really completes it. I gave this a 10.', '2006-12-06 15:11:30.000000', NULL, 0),
